    "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm having a bit trouble to understand where the error arises from. Just to be sure: You are installing from a jupyter notebook. Is this notebook in the same directory as the tequila source code (thats the directory where you cloned the code from which contains the folders 'src' and 'tutorials' etc and which has the files 'setup.py' and the modified 'requirements.txt'\r\n\r\nCould you try installing from command line:\r\n\r\ncd into the directory where you cloned tequila (the one where setup.py is)\r\nactivate your python environment (if you use one) \r\nthen type \r\n\r\npip install --upgrade -r requirements.txt\r\npip install -e .\r\n\r\n(requirements.txt should be the modified file, and don't forget the \".\" in the end of the second command)\r\n\r\nif no errors occur until that point, start python and try to import tequila\r\n\r\nIf this does not work: Can you post the error traceback here?",
